    "result_text": "The only remaining references are the tests asserting `membershipTier` **does not exist** \u2014 which is exactly the desired behaviour. The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133, capped, with level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`util/MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a shared helper `MembershipLevel.of(Owner)` that computes the level: start at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. Centralizing it keeps the response mapping and the audit line consistent.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `@Mapping` that derived the string tier (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) now derives `membershipLevel` via the helper. Deriving it in the mapper (from the persisted `namesakeCount` + `email`) is required because `GET /owners/{id}` re-fetches the entity, and those fields are fixed at creation.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `membershipTier` string property from the `Owner` schema and added `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 4). This regenerates `OwnerDto` so the old field is gone from the response and the new one appears.\n\n4. **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` alongside the id it already logged, using the same helper.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 34 tests, 0 failures. This includes the behaviour-change tests: Cp15/Cp24 (email + namesake 0 \u2192 level 3), Cp23 (no email, namesake 0 \u2192 level 2, GOLD tier gone), and Cp21 (audit line records the numeric level), plus every other existing test.",
